      "round": 2,
      "round_summary": "Round 2/3: Fix dut_bug in barrel shifter stages 2-5. Root cause: stages 2 (tmp2), 3 (tmp3), 4 (tmp4), 5 (tmp5) all read from tmp0 instead of chaining from the previous stage's result (tmp1, tmp2, tmp3, tmp4 respectively). This caused the effective rotation to be determined solely by the highest-order set bit in io.amount instead of the cumulative sum. Fix: changed Cat() operands in stages 2-5 to read from the preceding stage (tmp1→tmp2→tmp3→tmp4→tmp5 pipeline chain). The assertion label \"barrel_shifter_correct_ror\" is preserved exactly. No homologous assertions (the bug was in DUT wiring, not in assertion patterns). This fix also addresses the other two failing properties (dout_equals_shifter_output and spin_nonzero_rotation_changes_value) since they depend on correct tmp5 computation.",
